{"items":[{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate the OntoGraph research work needed to turn existing research artifacts into an organised gold corpus for model design, extraction examples, evaluation, and future training.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#237\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#245\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#246\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#247\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":5,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph gold corpus foundation","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/5"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7k0","labels":["epic","ontograph","gold-corpus"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph gold corpus foundation"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate definition of loadable cognitive/perspective model packages that guide agent questioning, extraction, mapping, and output language.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#238\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#248\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#249\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#255\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#256\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#257\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":6,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph cognitive model package system","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/6"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7lQ","labels":["epic","ontograph","cognitive-models"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph cognitive model package system"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate the governed source-to-canonical pipeline for turning source artifacts and model-language statements into reviewable canonical candidates.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#239\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#250\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#258\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":7,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph source-to-canonical pipeline","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/7"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7mA","labels":["epic","ontograph","canonicalisation"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph source-to-canonical pipeline"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate the lens/runtime work that lets agents communicate in a user/model/domain language while storing mapped understanding in canonical OntoGraph form.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#240\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#272\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#273\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#274\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#275\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":8,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph perspective and language lens runtime","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/8"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7mg","labels":["epic","ontograph","cognitive-models","canonicalisation"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph perspective and language lens runtime"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate sentinel-agent behaviour so agents can explore permitted enterprise knowledge, ask people and other agents better questions, detect gaps/staleness/conflicts, and propose mapped knowledge into OntoGraph.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#241\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#251\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#259\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#260\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#261\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":9,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph sentinel agent network","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/9"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7nQ","labels":["epic","ontograph","cognitive-models","sentinel-agents"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph sentinel agent network"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate coverage/staleness/telemetry work so OntoGraph can show explored, unexplored, stale, disputed, weakly evidenced, heavily used, and review-ready areas.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#242\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#252\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#262\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#263\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#264\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":10,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph coverage, staleness, and usage telemetry","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/10"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7no","labels":["epic","ontograph","telemetry"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph coverage, staleness, and usage telemetry"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate evaluation data and benchmarks for extraction quality before any custom/fine-tuned OntoUML-aware model is trained.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#243\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#254\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#269\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#270\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#271\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":11,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph evaluation and future OntoUML-aware training","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/11"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7n8","labels":["epic","ontograph","evaluation"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph evaluation and future OntoUML-aware training"},{"content":{"body":"## Outcome\nCoordinate the first end-to-end value-planning sentinel slice proving loaded model -> questions -> extraction -> canonical mapping -> gaps -> coverage report.\n\n## Linked OntoGraph research epic\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#244\n\n## Linked research task issues\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#253\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#265\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#266\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#267\n- governance-foundation/ontograph-research#268\n\n## Orchestration role\nThis Governance Foundation work-agents epic tracks assignment, sequencing, review, and closure. Detailed research artifacts and implementation notes remain in ontograph-research.\n\n## Source planning docs\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-epics.md\n- https://github.com/governance-foundation/ontograph-research/blob/main/docs/cognitive-model-sentinel-task-breakdown.md\n","number":12,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"Epic: OntoGraph first thin slice — value-planning sentinel","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/12"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgss7oo","labels":["epic","ontograph","cognitive-models","sentinel-agents","thin-slice"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"Epic: OntoGraph first thin slice — value-planning sentinel"},{"content":{"body":"## Delivery mode\n\nAgent-ops / operating-contract update.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe OntoGraph developer cron contract currently tells `ontograph_developer` to select eligible open `dev` issues from Governance Foundation Project #1, but it does not explicitly require Project Status transitions when an issue is selected, PR work starts, completion occurs, or a blocker is found.\n\nThis leaves a governance gap: an issue can be actively worked while the board still appears to be in Backlog or Ready, making the queue misleading for the operator and for later worker runs.\n\n## Source-of-truth files to inspect\n\nUpdate the source contract in `governance-foundation/work-agents`, not the OntoGraph product repo.\n\nRequired files to inspect before editing:\n\n- `README.md`\n- `profiles/governance-foundation.md`\n- `docs/governance-developer-agent-standing-prompt.md`\n- `docs/ontograph-developer-cron-bootstrap.md`\n- `docs/communication-map.md`\n- `docs/source-of-truth-sync.md`\n- `docs/spec-first-execution-contract.md`\n- `docs/dirty-worktree-and-handoff-policy.md`\n- `docs/evidence-checklist.md`\n\nRelevant existing contract points:\n\n- `docs/ontograph-developer-cron-bootstrap.md` identifies the OntoGraph board, tells the worker to select open `dev` issues whose Project Status is not Done/Blocked/Parked, and requires issue comments plus durable handoff evidence.\n- `.governance` / VibeGov workflow requires board state to follow actual delivery state: Backlog -> Ready -> In progress -> In review -> Done, with Blocked used for proven blockers.\n- `docs/communication-map.md` says the developer worker selects top project-list `dev` issues and should not manually force Project Status to Done.\n\n## Desired outcome\n\nThe OntoGraph developer worker contract must explicitly define Project Status handling for issue pickup and delivery state changes.\n\nAfter this issue is complete, a worker/operator reading only `work-agents` docs should know exactly when the worker must attempt to move an OntoGraph Project #1 item to:\n\n- `Ready`\n- `In progress`\n- `In review`\n- `Blocked`\n- `Done`\n\nand exactly what to do when board mutation is not available.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nUpdate the docs so the OntoGraph developer cron follows these rules:\n\n### Selection / pickup\n\nWhen selecting a new issue from a clean/current `develop` state:\n\n1. Confirm the issue is open, `dev`, not Done/Blocked/Parked, and has an executable deliverable.\n2. If the issue is under-specified or has no executable deliverable, do not start implementation. Comment the reason and set/mark it Blocked when possible, or leave it unready with a clear handoff if board mutation is unavailable.\n3. When the issue is selected for active work, attempt to set Project #1 Status to `In progress` before or immediately after the durable start/resume issue comment.\n4. The start/resume comment must state whether the status transition succeeded, failed, or was not available.\n\n### Branch / implementation\n\nWhen an issue branch is created or resumed:\n\n1. Status should remain `In progress`.\n2. Issue/branch/PR comments must include branch name, intended deliverable, planned files/specs/tests, and expected validation evidence.\n\n### PR / review\n\nWhen a PR is opened for the issue:\n\n1. Attempt to set Project #1 Status to `In review`.\n2. If Project mutation fails, leave a PR or issue comment with the exact failure and continue normal PR evidence handling.\n3. Do not claim review state from PR existence alone unless the status transition or mutation blocker is recorded.\n\n### Blocker\n\nWhen work cannot proceed:\n\n1. Attempt to set Project #1 Status to `Blocked`.\n2. Leave an issue comment with blocker summary, impact, attempted validation/proof, exact missing decision/prerequisite, and next safe action.\n3. If board mutation fails, the issue comment must say `Project status update blocked` and include evidence.\n\n### Completion\n\nWhen the issue is merged and closed:\n\n1. Do not manually force Project Status to `Done` unless the documented project workflow explicitly allows it.\n2. Record the closed issue, merged PR, commit hash, validation evidence, and cleanup state as completion proof.\n3. If automation does not move the item to `Done`, record that as a board automation gap rather than silently editing the status.\n\n### No-work stand-down\n\nIf no eligible queued work exists:\n\n1. Preserve the existing no-work behaviour: disable the cron by patching `enabled=false` and do not remove/delete the cron.\n2. Record the no-work/stand-down evidence in the configured visible Telegram update and durable handoff surface.\n3. If a control issue exists for this mode, comment there with queue state and disabled cron id.\n\n## Required documentation updates\n\nAt minimum, update:\n\n1. `docs/ontograph-developer-cron-bootstrap.md`\n   - add a `Project Status transition rule` section\n   - update the startup loop to include status transition attempts\n   - update final/blocked/PR behaviour to record status transition results\n\n2. `docs/governance-developer-agent-standing-prompt.md`\n   - align the generic issue lifecycle with the cron-specific Project Status rule\n   - make explicit that Project Status mutation attempts must be reported in issue/PR comments\n\n3. `docs/communication-map.md`\n   - update the `ontograph_developer` role text so it no longer only says it selects top project-list `dev` issues, but also attempts Project Status transitions at pickup/PR/blocker/completion boundaries\n   - preserve the rule that the worker must not manually force Done unless explicitly allowed\n\n4. `docs/source-of-truth-sync.md`\n   - update the cron update checklist so any cron payload refresh must verify Project Status transition wording is present\n\nUpdate `README.md` only if the active-agent summary becomes inaccurate after the above changes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Changing OntoGraph product code.\n- Changing OntoGraph product issues except where used as examples in docs.\n- Implementing GitHub Project API tooling.\n- Editing live OpenClaw cron payloads directly unless a follow-up issue explicitly owns runtime sync.\n- Changing the rule that implementation evidence belongs in the owning target repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The OntoGraph developer cron docs explicitly require attempting `In progress` on issue pickup.\n- The docs explicitly require attempting `In review` when a PR is opened.\n- The docs explicitly require attempting `Blocked` when work is blocked.\n- The docs preserve the existing rule not to manually force `Done` unless explicitly allowed.\n- The docs specify exactly what comment/handoff evidence is required when Project Status mutation succeeds, fails, or is unavailable.\n- The docs specify the behaviour for under-specified/no-deliverable issues so the worker does not start poor-quality issues.\n- The cron update checklist includes Project Status transition wording as a required sync check.\n- No product-repo behaviour or OntoGraph semantics are changed by this issue.\n\n## Verification expectations\n\nUse documentation validation appropriate to the repo.\n\nExpected checks:\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- search check proving the new wording exists in each touched file, for example:\n  - `rg \"Project Status transition|In progress|In review|Blocked\" docs README.md profiles`\n- direct review that no example uses a real person name in durable ticket text\n- direct review that Telegram/session targets remain fully qualified where examples are touched\n\nIf local commands cannot run, record the blocker and provide exact manual inspection evidence in the PR.\n\n## Required PR evidence\n\nThe PR body must include:\n\n- Issue: closes this issue\n- Files changed\n- Summary of Project Status transition rules added\n- Why no target-repo implementation change was made\n- Validation/proof commands and results\n- Any residual runtime-sync gap, especially if live cron payloads still need refreshing from the updated docs\n- PR link, final commit hash, and final issue comment evidence\n\n## Follow-up expected if not done in this issue\n\nIf this issue only updates source docs and does not update the live OpenClaw cron payload, create/link a follow-up issue for runtime sync validation. That follow-up must verify the actual `ontograph_developer` cron payload is aligned with the updated source docs before claiming operational completion.","number":13,"repository":"governance-foundation/work-agents","title":"OntoGraph dev cron: enforce GitHub Project status transitions","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents/issues/13"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgxbdeQ","labels":["enhancement","doc","agent-ops","priority:p0"],"repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/work-agents","status":"Todo","title":"OntoGraph dev cron: enforce GitHub Project status transitions"},{"content":{"body":"## Problem\n\n`agent.txt` is intended to be a canonical agent-readable entry point, but two things make it harder to trust and inspect:\n\n1. It appears to render as a single long line rather than a readable plain-text contract.\n2. It includes a role bootstrap URL shaped like `https://vibegov.io/roles//BOOTSTRAP.md`, which looks like a missing role placeholder.\n\nBecause agents may consume this file directly, the format and URL pattern should be unambiguous.\n\n## Affected areas\n\nLikely affected file/output:\n\n- `static/agent.txt`\n- any docs that reference the role bootstrap URL pattern\n- any generation script if `agent.txt` is generated\n\n## Recommended fix\n\nMake `agent.txt` multiline and human-inspectable while remaining agent-readable.\n\nReplace the broken role URL with an explicit placeholder pattern such as:\n\n```text\nhttps://vibegov.io/roles/{role}/BOOTSTRAP.md\n```\n\nIf the intended pattern is different, document the exact supported role bootstrap URL shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `agent.txt` renders as readable multiline plain text.\n- [ ] No URL contains `roles//BOOTSTRAP.md`.\n- [ ] The role bootstrap URL pattern is explicit and valid.\n- [ ] Agents and humans can determine how to fetch role-specific bootstrap instructions.\n- [ ] Any related docs use the same URL pattern.\n\n## Priority\n\nP0 — canonical agent entrypoint correctness.","number":155,"repository":"governance-foundation/vibegov.io","title":"Fix agent.txt formatting and role bootstrap URL","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/vibegov.io/issues/155"},"id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgxeXa8","repository":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/vibegov.io","status":"In Progress","title":"Fix agent.txt formatting and role bootstrap URL"}],"totalCount":10}
